						<tr>
							<td height="50" colspan="3" valign="top" class="windowbg2" align="left"><div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1606.msg17673#msg17673">Quote from: DepravenSoul on June 30, 2005, 12:31:42 am</a></div><div class="quote">to be able to log on every night to the same character, playing at the end level game, raiding with the same group of friends, and always having raid targets available to hit is what sells the high end game I think. I am somewhat curious as to how the high end game of the latest expansion has turned out to be.<br /></div><br />I&#039;m not one to jump in on discussions like these - I&#039;m not verbose enough or knowledgeable enough to make educated statements. (Although some people are worse than I am and yap their fingers off. This thread seems rather civil though, for once. ;))<br /><br />Anyways, I agree completely with Depraven. While Union of Power isn&#039;t in the end-game content of today, we are in the end-game content of a few years ago - one zone that many EQ players still will never see. And that&#039;s something we&#039;re damn proud of. It&#039;s this fact that makes me log in every night. It&#039;s to talk with the same friends I&#039;ve talked with and been guilded with (in some form or another) for the past 4.5 years. Hell, the last week in July a bunch of us are gathering in RL for a week of playing together - it&#039;ll be the first time I&#039;ll have met them, although I&#039;ve known them for 4.5 years.<br /><br />Until all my friends leave, there&#039;s only 1 EQ server and it really *is* run by a hampster, or I lose my job and home and all worldly possessions and can&#039;t pay for a subscription, (although I&#039;ll be panhandling with a cardboard sign that says &quot;Please help. Need $ for MMORPG addiction.&quot;), I&#039;ll stay faithful to EQ. I was never one for branching out, anyways - that&#039;s why I&#039;ve only ever leveled one character up past 25.<br /><br />On topic of the WoW subscriptors - I have two close friends whom for *years* chided and taunted me about my MMORPG (and subsiquent EQ) addiction. Now both are hopelessly addicted to WoW and I laugh at them. Fuckin&#039; hypocrites.<br /><br />Wow, that&#039;s the most I&#039;ve ever typed on this board.<br /><br />Cheers.</td>
